title: 'pallet-revive: keep an unreleased storage deposit refund refundable'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    On a runtime using `PGasDeposit`, the native part of a refund for removed contract storage is released only to an account that paid a storage deposit for the contract in native currency, and only up to what it paid. When a different account removes that storage, the backend leaves the native part on the contract's hold, but the contract's recorded storage deposit was already lowered by the full refund. The unreleased amount stayed on hold and could only leave it at contract termination, paid to the terminating origin.

    The amount the hold exceeds the recorded storage deposit by is now paid out with the next storage removal by an account that paid a native deposit for the contract, up to what that account paid, to its free balance. It is not part of the storage deposit the call reports. Amounts stranded on existing contracts before this change are paid out the same way; no migration is needed.

    `Deposit` gains the method `refund_excess`, which pays such an amount from a contract's hold. The trait is sealed, so no downstream implementation needs updating.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: minor
